LMS-FILL: fix for #12
https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/12

fill_rand() is told nodes_0+nodes_1+1 = nodes_0+2 weights, but the array holds nodes_0+1,
so it writes one weight past the end (heap overrun). Under DOS it clobbers errors[0]; on macOS
malloc can abort. No other effect on results.

Applies to the sources prepared by src/tools/prepare.py (wrapped lines rejoined,
names lower-cased), not to src/borland/ directly:
  patch -p1 -d <prep dir> < src/fixes/LMS-FILL.patch

--- a/lms.c
+++ b/lms.c
@@ -86,7 +86,9 @@
 
 /* Initialise the network */
 
+               /* Fix #12: fill_rand wrote one weight past the end of the array
+                * https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/12 */
-               fill_rand(ann.layer_1, ann.nodes_0+ann.nodes_1+1, ann.nodes_1);
+               fill_rand(ann.layer_1, ann.nodes_0+1, ann.nodes_1);
 
 /* Set start bit */
 
